  "id": "nested-checked-record-browser-ordinary-full-installed",
  "kind": "installed",
  "revision": "340f6c1dabd1cad6fa313c41682c9b2c3fd08d24",
  "command": "LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_BROWSER_TEST=1 LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_BROWSER_ROUTES='ordinary-full' LEAN_BRIDGE_NESTED_CHECKED_RECORD_BROWSER_OUTPUT=/app/build/vo1477-nested-checked-record-npm-r1 LEAN_BRIDGE_TYPE_CORPUS_BROWSERS=chromium,firefox,webkit node --test --test-concurrency=1 tests/nested-checked-record-browser.test.mjs",
  "scope": "Two independent author builds reproduce complete component and runtime archives before source-free offline npm installation. Installed JavaScript and strict TypeScript callers replay after physical relocation. Chromium, Firefox and WebKit each execute page, React production/Strict Mode and dedicated-worker consumers, including missing-Wasm recovery, for twelve browser executions and fifty-one lifecycle observations. The full package checks direct and repeated parameters plus Array, List, Option, Product, Except, enclosing record and active variant fields; exact failures preserve caller graphs and later calls recover. Producer, browser-consumer and destructive-checker revisions are independently frozen. Nested checked-record acceptance covers only the tested acyclic Packet, Holder and Choice forms through Array, List, Option, Product and Except copy positions. Generic, recursive and inherited records, other index kinds, open dependent or zero-payload records, callbacks and owned positions remain unreviewed. Other host targets require their own installed evidence. These local Linux x64 Node, strict TypeScript, Chromium, Firefox and WebKit runs do not establish hosted acceptance. Constructor dispatch counts and peak memory are unmeasured. Complete npm component/runtime archives and original report inputs are retained; browser binaries, React framework archives and generated deployments are represented by recorded identities and observations rather than copied.",
